{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Is not Aaron your brother the Levite?</b> If the intent was to send one qualified to speak, is not Aaron your brother — who is a Levite, undeniably a man of wisdom like all his Levite brethren — available?" "<b>I know that he can speak.</b> He himself is by nature a man of practiced tongue." "<b>And also, behold, he is coming out to meet you, and he will see you and rejoice in his heart.</b> And even though he comes out to meet you to honor you on account of your superiority over him, he will undoubtedly rejoice, and he will be for you an interpreter with a whole heart."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:21.379269024Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}